SQLite is in the Public Domain
==============================

SQLite ships no separate licence file. The author's disclaimer and blessing are
carried in the header of every SQLite source file, and are reproduced here
verbatim so that the vendored tree states its own terms without anyone having to
scroll nine million lines of amalgamation to find them:

    2001-09-15

    The author disclaims copyright to this source code.  In place of
    a legal notice, here is a blessing:

       May you do good and not evil.
       May you find forgiveness for yourself and forgive others.
       May you share freely, never taking more than you give.

Vendored release: SQLite 3.53.4
Source id:        2026-07-24 19:02:57
                  bf7c7f30031888f4e796e429ab3978879485813aaca6f641c7b33e4e09459bcc
Upstream:         https://sqlite.org

Public domain means there is no attribution obligation and no licence text to
propagate. This file exists anyway, because a vendored dependency whose terms are
not written down beside it is a dependency somebody will have to research under
pressure later.
